   802 				;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   803 				; Load_Menu_Banner_Raw - boot-time load of the static menu banner pixel data
   804 				; (D:MENU.RAW - the logo) into dedicated, resident VRAM - never touched by Load_Image,
   805 				; and never reloaded from disk again after this one call, since the banner
   806 				; never changes at runtime.  Blank-fills any banner target whose file is
   807 				; missing/fails so cold-boot VRAM garbage is never shown.  The separator has
   808 				; no disk file - its 160-byte pattern table is assembly-embedded straight into
   809 				; MENU_SEP_VRAM at load time (Load_Menu_Sep, init_vbxe.asm).  The banner's palette (registers 1-3) is no longer a disk
   810 				; asset - see Load_Menu_Ramps (init_vbxe.asm), assembly-embedded directly into
   811 				; MENU_BANNER_PAL_VRAM.  Called once from start:, before the first
   812 				; Enter_Selector.
   813 				;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   814 3506			Load_Menu_Banner_Raw
   815 				; The ANTIC loading screen is still up (start: turns DMA off afterwards), so
   816 				; this load reports on it like the init stages: message on row 3, then the
