  1116 				;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1117 				; Fill_Pal_Preview_Cmap - stage the P-preview's 2x2 grid into CRAM_Buffer
  1118 				; (TL is left at the buffer's zero default = palette 0) then expand the
  1119 				; whole buffer into real CRAM via the existing Setup_Cmap1.  Called once
  1120 				; from Selector_Handle_P (ui.asm).
  1121 				;
  1122 				; Repurposes BLT_MENU_SEP_CLEAR (bcbs.asm) rather than adding a 13th BCB -
  1123 				; it was the separator's boot-time constant fill, but the separator is now a
  1124 				; 160-byte table loaded straight into VRAM (Load_Menu_Sep, init_vbxe.asm), so
  1125 				; this is its only user.  The 12 BCBs already in bcbs.asm exactly fill the
  1126 				; $100-$1FF VBXE VRAM budget (see the memory-map comment at the top of this
  1127 				; file); a 13th BCB overflowed BLT_NFO_NAME_CLEAR across the $200 boundary
